{#
==============================================================
DRUPAL PREPROCESS ALTERNATIVE (recommended for Drupal projects)
==============================================================
If this template is used inside a full Drupal theme (not standalone),
you should NOT include the full <html>/<head> structure above.
Instead, strip everything down to just the <main> content and
add GA via your theme's .theme file:

In mytheme.theme:

function mytheme_preprocess_node(&$variables) {
  if ($variables['node']->bundle() === 'gfci') {
    $gtag_id = 'G-9WWD1TRBQN';

    $variables['#attached']['html_head'][] = [
      [
        '#type' => 'html_tag',
        '#tag' => 'script',
        '#attributes' => [
          'async' => TRUE,
          'src' => 'https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=' . $gtag_id,
        ],
      ],
      'google_gtag_script',
    ];

    $variables['#attached']['html_head'][] = [
      [
        '#type' => 'html_tag',
        '#tag' => 'script',
        '#value' => "window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);}
gtag('js', new Date());
gtag('config', '" . $gtag_id . "');",
      ],
      'google_gtag_init',
    ];
  }
}

Then in node--gfci.html.twig, only keep the <header>, <main>, and <footer>
content — Drupal's html.html.twig handles <head> automatically.
==============================================================
#}
